# GEPER Docker/docker-compose environment file example.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory (docker-compose loads
# `.env` automatically; a plain `docker run` needs `--env-file .env` or
# individual `-e` flags) and fill in real values. `.env` itself is
# gitignored (see .gitignore) -- never commit real credentials here or
# anywhere else in this repo. This file exists so a new user has the
# variable names to copy instead of reconstructing them from
# DOCKER.md's prose (G3, report review round 5).
#
# Nothing here is required to build/run the image -- every value below
# is read with a safe empty-string default (see docker-compose.yml's
# `environment:` block and geper/config.py). GEPER degrades gracefully
# without any of these: NCBI E-utilities works unauthenticated (at a
# lower, shared rate limit -- see geper/utils/ncbi_eutils.py), BLAST
# falls back to remote/skip, and AlphaMissense downloads its catalogue
# on first use instead of using a pre-provisioned local copy.

# --- NCBI E-utilities (ClinVar/dbSNP queries) ---------------------------
# A real email is NCBI's own usage-policy requirement for any
# non-trivial query volume (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK25497/)
# -- geper/config.py's own committed default is a placeholder
# (geper.pipeline@example.com) that geper/utils/ncbi_eutils.py warns
# about at startup specifically so nobody mistakes it for a real,
# usable value in production.
GEPER_NCBI_EMAIL=

# Raises NCBI's rate limit from 3 req/s (unauthenticated) to 10 req/s.
# Get one at https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/account/settings/ (free NCBI
# account, "API Key Management").
GEPER_NCBI_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: pre-provisioned local data (skip GEPER's own auto-download) ---
# Path/prefix of a local BLAST+ database, if you already have one built
# (see README.md section 20). Leave unset to let GEPER fall back to
# remote NCBI BLAST or skip BLAST entirely.
GEPER_BLAST_DATABASE=

# Paths to pre-downloaded AlphaMissense catalogue slices (hg38/hg19),
# if you already have one, instead of letting GEPER download the
# multi-GB catalogue itself on first use.
GEPER_ALPHAMISSENSE_HG38_LOCAL=
GEPER_ALPHAMISSENSE_HG19_LOCAL=

# --- Cache location (already set inside the image; override only if
# you want the container's model/dataset caches somewhere other than
# the geper_model_cache Docker volume -- see the Dockerfile's own
# comment on its GEPER_CACHE_DIR line, and geper/config.py) ---
# GEPER_CACHE_DIR=/app/geper/model_cache

# --- kim_pipeline/api/main.py -- REQUIRED before a real deployment (FIX #3) ---
# The API server will not start without both of these set, unless
# GEPER_DEV_INSECURE=1 is set instead (dev/test only -- see
# kim_pipeline/docs/INSTALL.md's "Start the API Server" section).
# GEPER_API_KEYS=key1,key2
# GEPER_CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.example.com
# GEPER_DEV_INSECURE=1
